          "date": "2026-11-04 18:02:45.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-19566 lfsck: clear the header of a rebuilt LOV EA",
        "message": "LU-19566 lfsck: clear the header of a rebuilt LOV EA\n\nWhen LFSCK rebuilds a composite LOV EA for an orphan OST object\nin lfsck_layout_new_comp_lovea(), the buffer holds the crashed\nLOV EA being replaced or, when creating the LOV EA, whatever\nlti_big_buf last held (linkEA, LMV).  Only some of the\nlov_comp_md_v1 header fields were set, so lcm_ec_count and the\npadding fields kept those bytes, and without a layout version\nfrom the OST, lcm_layout_gen was incremented from them as well.\n\nClear the whole header and the first entry before filling them.\nKeep lcm_layout_gen only when replacing an existing LOV EA.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-lfsck\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I951b3a96d5c0670e1296557ce1a597fda23ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
